# Agda scratch probes.  Agents testing whether something reduces on the nose
# write throwaway modules; two of these (`ZZTestSolver.agda`, `Probe1.agda`)
# were swept into commits by `git add -A` and had to be removed again.  A
# probe is a question, not a result: name it `Probe*.agda` or `Scratch*.agda`
# and it stays out of the tree.  Anything worth keeping goes in
# `NaturalMachine/` under a name that carries its category.
formal/cubical/Probe*.agda
formal/cubical/Tmp*.agda
formal/cubical/**/Tmp*.agda
formal/cubical/Scratch*.agda
formal/cubical/**/Probe*.agda
formal/cubical/**/Scratch*.agda
runtime/LIVING_RUN.log
runtime/LIVING_STATE.json
vigil-state.json
zzz/natural_machine_cpu_loop_rust/real_workload
zzz/natural_machine_cpu_loop_rust/decic_extend
zzz/natural_machine_cpu_loop_rust/root_singular_series
formal/cubical/Candidate_*.agda

# interactive/library.terms is NOT ignored, and used to be, listed right here
# among the reproducible artifacts.  It is the opposite of one: it is the
# machine's MEMORY, the file MathMachine reads at startup to re-admit what
# earlier runs proved.  Ignored, it never left the container that wrote it,
# so every fresh checkout — every CI job, every new session, every future
# scheduled run — started the machine from mRules = [] and re-derived the
# same theorems forever.  The engine's own comment says the architecture
# "rests on installed theorems compounding"; nothing can compound across a
# clone that does not carry the file.  Tracked as of 2026-08-17.

# Machine build artifacts (reproducible; never source of truth)
interactive/*.hi
interactive/*.o
interactive/arithvocab
interactive/bench-head-depth
interactive/cyclotomic-vocab
interactive/parallel-gate
interactive/library.certs
interactive/self_architecture.tsv
interactive/nested-agda/

# Certificate gate cache: re-derivable, and every entry stores the exact
# module source it certified, so it is a rebuildable artifact not a record.
interactive/.certcache/
formal/cubical/.claude/
interactive/replay.traces.live

# The sabhā: the compiled process and its transcript.  The binary is
# rebuildable from interactive/check-sabha.sh; the transcript is a session
# record, kept locally and never rewritten in place (append-only), and it
# is the corpus this wire exists to produce.
interactive/sabha
interactive/sabha.jsonl

# The interface the other carrier is handed: the compiled binary, rebuildable
# from interactive/check-karana.sh.  Its outputs (the tool schema, the training
# records) are regenerated from the running dispatch table and a transcript,
# so neither is committed either -- a committed copy would be the second copy
# that drifts, which is the thing this lane exists to remove.
interactive/karana
interactive/abhyasa.jsonl
**/.certcache/

# compiled binaries — build output, rebuilt in place by interactive/check-*.sh; never track
interactive/math-machine
interactive/repairfixpoint
interactive/question-machine

# cabal's build tree, created in the repo root by
# scripts/Dhruva_TheDeclaredPinIsBuiltFromNothingOrTheRunSaysWhichItGot.sh
# when it builds the pinned Agda 2.8.0.  A build artifact, never a claim.
dist-newstyle/

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PURIFICATION, 2026-08-25, owner: "gitignore build artifacts logs etc."
#
# Everything above this line was written one path at a time, by whoever
# happened to compile something new, which is why it lists four binaries
# by name and misses the fifth.  These are the general rules.  A build
# artifact is reproducible from a command in the tree; a log and a
# transcript are records of ONE CONTAINER and do not survive the clone
# they were written in.  Neither is a claim, and neither is source.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# compiled output, any lane, any depth
*.hi
*.o
*.agdai
*.dyn_hi
*.dyn_o
*.so
*.a

# logs and per-run transcripts
*.log
*.jsonl

# the archive is history, not working state: nothing here is built,
# checked, imported or run.  It is kept so `git log` and `git show`
# still answer, and so a claim can be traced to the script it came from.
zzz/**/*.pyc

# interactive/yantra-session.lekha — the per-run session defect log.
# run-yantra.sh does `rm -f "$LEKHA"` on EVERY invocation, by design: its
# own header says the chain must start at genesis so that `dosa.pramanya`
# verifies THIS run and not a history it did not produce.  So a committed
# copy is, by construction, always some other container's run — and a
# `--wire` session deletes it and writes nothing, which is how it showed
# up as a staged deletion.  interactive/dosa.lekha, the shared append-only
# log several lanes write to, is a different file and stays tracked.
interactive/yantra-session.lekha
formal/cubical/corpus/Chunk*.agda
formal/cubical/corpus/identity-rows.tsv
formal/cubical/corpus/corpus-rows.tsv
CorpusProbe.generated.agda
formal/cubical/CensusB.agda*

